		(uuid "44c86911-1e53-5b81-832f-8db19fae0f95")
	)
	(text "Two n8synth-style edge strips, 40 positions each at 2.54 mm. Each position is an outer hole (the deck's\nheader pin) joined to an inner hole (a wiring point): both pads carry the same pad number, so they share a net.\nNothing on the board connects to them: each module is wired by hand from the channel holes to the inner\nholes. Deck cells occupy positions 1-10, 16-25 and 31-40; 11-15 and 26-30 are free tie points.\n10HP: the board sits parallel behind the deck and both strips are used. 6HP: the board sits at 90° and\nonly the left strip meets the deck's right-angle header."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 22.86 0)
		(effects
			(font (size 1.5 1.5))
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "9561d0d3-d9c0-54f8-b5e2-be94e2d2bb28")
	)
